[Much discussion about the Terminator race in NetHack deleted.]

Why wimp out?  Let's have a few 'C' CorDhumps running around.  They are
at least twice as fast as you, you can never escape them.  The attack of
the ferocious CorDhump can often kill an adventurer in one round. They cannot 
be genocided, polymorphed, disabled  or killed in any fashion.  They can
appear on any level, and can climb the stairs to follow you.  Any critter
can invoke the CorDhump for protection.

One critter already does.  The long worm invokes the CorDhump when you,
as a marilith, attack it's tail.  (Try it.)  :-)

Seriously, we don't need Terminators or CorDhumps, and even more powerful
weapons to deal with even more powerful monsters.  A pong game at 1 point
per hit is as fun as a pong game at 10,000 points per hit.  NetHack should
be a nice balanced game.  Let's not continuously try to out-do ourselves
with more powerful monsters and weapons.  Let's not lose sight of the implicit
charter of NetHack. (A Tolkienesque/AD&D look and feel.) 

We can still breathe new life into NetHack without making it a potpourri of
genres and escalating weapon and monster classes...

